            "execution_time_sec": 274.2299407690007,
            "final_response_preview": "Fix applied to /app/user.cpp: Pre-initialize iostream/locale internals in user_init() so\nthat libstdc++ lazy allocations happen BEFORE the program installs its custom global\nheap (g_custom_heap). This prevents standard-library allocations from using the\ncustom heap and being freed or accessed after that heap is destroyed, which caused\na release-only SIGSEGV. Only /app/user.cpp was modified (per constraints).\n\nWhat changed (summary):\n- user_init() now does lightweight operations that force std::iostream internals to\n  initialize: creates/uses an ostringstream, imbues std::cout with the default\n  locale, and touches std::cout.rdbuf().\n\nHow to reproduce / verify:\n1) Release build:\n   g++ -std=c++17 -o /app/release /app/main.cpp /app/user.cpp -O2 -DNDEBUG \\\n       -L/usr/local/gcc-custom-release/lib64 -Wl,-Bstatic -lstdc++ -Wl,-Bdynamic -lm\n   Run: /app/release  (exits 0, no crash)\n\n2) Valgrind check:\n   valgrind --leak-check=full --show-leak-kinds=all /app/release\n   Result: ERROR SUMMARY"
        }
